              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Types and Init",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Statically typed==: every variable's type is fixed at compile time",
                "Sizes are implementation-defined: `int` >= 16 bits (typically 32), `long long` >= 64",
                "Exact width: `int32_t`, `uint64_t` from `<cstdint>`",
                "`auto x = 5;` deduces `int`, drops top-level const and references"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Init",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`int x{5};`",
                  "{green:OK}"
                ],
                [
                  "`int x{3.5};`",
                  "{red:error}: narrowing rejected"
                ],
                [
                  "`int x = 3.5;`",
                  "silently truncates to 3"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. const and constexpr",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`const int n = 10;` is read-only after init and ==must be initialized==",
                "`constexpr` also needs a ==compile-time== value",
                "So it can size arrays: `constexpr int N = 8; int a[N];`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Declaration",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`const int* p`",
                  "pointer to const data: no `*p = ...`"
                ],
                [
                  "`int* const p`",
                  "const pointer: cannot reseat `p`"
                ],
                [
                  "`const int* const p`",
                  "both fixed"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Read right to left",
              "text": "`int* const p` reads: p is a ==const== pointer to int."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Signed `int` overflow is ==undefined behavior==",
                "`-1 < 1u` is **false**: the signed value converts to unsigned",
                "Uninitialized locals hold garbage: always initialize"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
