              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. C Array and Decay",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`int a[5] = {1,2,3};` ==fixed size==, contiguous",
                "Trailing elements zeroed ==only== with an initializer list",
                "No bounds check: `a[5]` is {red:UB}",
                "Passed to a function, it **decays** to `int*`",
                "`void f(int a[])` is really `void f(int* a)`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "int a[5]{};",
                "sizeof(a);   // 20, true array",
                "void f(int* p) { sizeof(p); }  // 8",
                "// pass the length: f(a, 5)"
              ],
              "note": "size is lost after decay"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. std::array",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`std::array<int,5> a{1,2,3,4,5};` zero-overhead wrapper",
                "Has `.size()`, range-for, copy by `=`",
                "`.at(i)` checks bounds, throws `std::out_of_range`",
                "{green:Does not decay}"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "C array",
                "std::array",
                "std::vector"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Size",
